    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      Manual Transfer Switch vs. Generator Interlock Kit: NEC Article 702
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      When connecting a portable generator to your residential electrical system, the National Electrical Code (NEC Article 702) requires a positive mechanical means to prevent simultaneous connection to both utility power and the generator. The two primary methods are a <strong>mechanical panel interlock kit</strong> and a <strong>multi-circuit manual transfer switch subpanel</strong>. Here is the technical breakdown of both systems.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 mb-6">
      <div>
