        solution: "Tape a laminated 'Emergency Outage Procedure' checklist to the panel deadfront detailing the exact steps to turn OFF heavy loads before switching to generator power."
      },
      {
        number: 3,
        title: "Running a 3-Wire (Ungrounded) Feeder to the Exterior Inlet Box",
        costImpact: "$1,600 (Electrocution Hazard & Repulling 4-Conductor Cable)",
        description: "Using old 10/2 with ground or omitting the insulated neutral conductor creates a shared return path that electrifies metal appliance casings during an outage.",
        solution: "Always install a 4-conductor feeder (two hots, one insulated neutral, and one equipment grounding conductor) between the inlet box and panel."
      }
    ]}
  />

